#
# Conformance case: contracts/closed-world-counterfactual-unsupported
# AC: a ReasoningContract that pairs closed-world closure
# (logic:ClosedWorldClosure, here the default closure) with counterfactual
# entrenchment revision (logic:EntrenchmentRevision) is a FORBIDDEN facet
# combination (RuleNoClosedWorldInCounterfactual): the counterfactual states the
# entrenchment revision generates are open-ended, so reading absence as falsehood
# inside them is unsound. The compile MUST emit an UNSUPPORTED_CONTRACT
# Severity::Error and the harness MUST short-circuit before evaluating — the
# "unsupported is a hard stop" guarantee, pinned at the corpus level (profile.json
# declares "expect_unsupported": true).
#
# This rule was previously only unit-tested; this case pins it at the corpus level
# alongside the other forbidden-combination cases.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/contracts/closed-world-counterfactual/> .

ex:UnsupportedContract a logic:ReasoningContract ;
    logic:defaultClosure logic:ClosedWorldClosure ;
    logic:revision logic:EntrenchmentRevision .
